report=['# Sequential reciprocal matching under uncertainty\n\nTechnical investigation, public release 1.0.0; 7 October 2026. All people and behavior are synthetic.']
report.append('## Abstract\n\nWe implemented an observation-only adaptive reciprocal policy, audited all ten public pools, executed a five-seed six-family ablation matrix, compared a separately selected candidate on fresh seeds, verified subprocess equivalence and ran an offline resource-limited container. The requested full architecture did **not** beat the reference greedy baseline. The frozen product-fusion candidate improved the fresh-seed point estimate, but uncertainty includes no improvement. Accordingly this report does not claim a statistically validated or globally optimal winning policy. Several requested premises are false for the shipped evaluator; correcting them materially changes stopping and information-elicitation conclusions.')
report.append('## 1. Executed scope and reproducibility\n\nThe original `kit.py`, `evaluate.py`, `policy.py`, public data and scratch research remain unchanged. `research_policy.py` is a separate JSON executable; `Dockerfile.research` packages it without datasets or research scripts. Legacy bibliography claims are archived in `research/legacy_references.md` and replaced by an applicability-audited bibliography in `docs/REFERENCES.md`. No hidden-world information crosses the policy boundary. Offline audit programs explicitly use simulator truth only for structural interventions and upper bounds.')
counts=[len(bench['episodes']),len(read('selection')['episodes']),len(hold['episodes']),len(sub['episodes']),len(queries['episodes']),len(hazard['episodes']),len(funnel['episodes']),len(container['episodes']),2]
report.append(f'Executed: {counts[0]} main ablation episodes, {counts[1]} selection episodes, {counts[2]} fresh-seed episodes, {counts[3]} official subprocess episodes, {counts[4]} query-comparison episodes, {counts[5]} explicit hazard-threshold episodes, {counts[6]} completed-funnel audit rollouts, {counts[7]} container episode and two host/container comparison rollouts. These are **{sum(counts)} recorded rollouts**, with intentional duplicate trajectories for protocol verification; they are not that many independent statistical observations. The two-worker benchmark uses `evaluate.episode` unchanged; fast mode substitutes only invocation with strict JSON serialization/validation. Every one of the 150 subprocess action digests equals its fast counterpart; the host/container semantic-action comparison agrees on every ask set and pair batch, with identical outcomes. The raw container digest differs because the order of asks within day 6 changes; this has no simulator effect and is not represented as byte-identical execution.')
report.append('The supplied six train, two validation and two development-test pools were used only for labeled descriptive audits, never to fit inference weights. They are day-30 snapshots, not early-day state reconstructions. Policy hyperparameter selection used seeds 201–203. Of seven prelisted configurations, product and FIFO tied at 0.305556; deterministic list order chose product. Fresh seeds 301–305 were evaluated after this choice, without retuning. Seeds 101–105 are exploratory benchmark seeds, not a pristine holdout, and existing scratch notes already examined some of them. No private-world performance is claimed.')
report.append('```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npython3 -m pip install -r requirements-research.txt\npython3 research/audit.py\npython3 research/upper_bound.py\npython3 research/benchmark.py\npython3 research/benchmark.py --policies full,greedy_engine,no_learning,zero,product,fifo,static --seeds 201,202,203 --output results/research/selection.json\npython3 research/benchmark.py --policies product,greedy,no_asks,random --seeds 301,302,303,304,305 --output results/research/holdout.json\npython3 research/benchmark.py --policies full,product,greedy,no_asks,random --subprocess --output results/research/subprocess.json\npython3 research/query_compare.py\npython3 research/funnel_audit.py\npython3 research/benchmark.py --policies hazard --output results/research/hazard.json\ndocker build -f Dockerfile.research -t sequential-research:1.0 .\npython3 research/container_check.py\npython3 research/compare_container.py\npython3 evaluate.py --image sequential-research:1.0 --seeds 101 --output results/research/container.json\npython3 -m unittest -v\npython3 -m unittest -v research.test_policy\npython3 verify_data.py\npython3 research/build_report.py\n```')
report.append('## 2. Simulator corrections and theoretical outcome\n\nActions run on days 0–59 and feedback continues through day 100. All possible public delays fit this follow-up window, so a day-60-only stopping cutoff is inappropriate for the official objective. Only 12% of agents have an exit in days 22–60; this is not a daily 12% hazard. Hard feasibility uses eleven fields, the constraints bundle costs three, and declined hard fields never become observed. A member can receive multiple distinct introductions after busy periods. `date_happened` is the actual feedback event name. Feedback is not delivered as `date_result`.')
report.append('The full information state is an MDP, but the observation interface requires a belief state. Overlapping dyads are not independent bandit arms; no Whittle indexability or exact Gittins reduction was proved. Node shadow prices exist for an LP relaxation, but odd-set prices and joint continuation values prevent a general exact separable reduction. A restricted immediate-stage zero-VoI proposition is proved below, along with a dynamic counterexample; graph expansion is not generally submodular. A correct one-stop Bellman recursion yields conditional monotonicity, not universal strict decline. Full derivations and proofs appear in Appendix A. References include [dynamic market thickness](https://doi.org/10.1086/704761), [Whittle](https://doi.org/10.2307/3214163), [Howard](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4082064/), [Blackwell](https://doi.org/10.1214/aoms/1177729032), and the online matching literature in the bibliography.')
report.append('### Oracle relaxation\n\nA time-indexed LP relaxes query budgets, long lockouts, retirement and integrality. It uses oracle non-declined hard constraints, true arrival/exit windows, pair-at-most-once and eight-day endpoint occupancy. The rewards integrate common dyadic randomness numerically. It bounds **expected** qualified reward under the stochastic model; it does not upper-bound a deterministic seed’s realized count. Values below are seed-101 latent-world relaxations, not directly comparable confidence limits on the five-seed sample means.\n\n'+table(['Family','Feasible edges','Variables','Expected MSMI/100 upper bound'],[(r['variant'],r.get('edges',0),r.get('variables',0),fmt(r['bound_msmi_per100'])) for r in upper]))
report.append('## 3. Public data audit\n\n### Reciprocal dependence\n\n'+table(['Population','Resolved pairs','Joint yes','Marginal product','Pearson rho','MI (bits)'],[(label,d['n'],fmt(d['p_both']),fmt(d['independent_product']),fmt(d['pearson']),fmt(d['mutual_information_bits'])) for label,d in [('No-response counts as nonacceptance',audit['public']['acceptance']),('Both members actually responded',audit['public']['acceptance_both_responded'])]]))
report.append('Joint distributions, all four contingency cells and per-pool estimates are in `audit.json`. These are exact sample frequencies for selected observed introductions, not exact latent population probabilities. Pending directional outcomes are excluded; explicit no-response is a nonacceptance in the first row. Arbitrary member-ID ordering defines A and B. Positive shared effects justify integrating reciprocal probabilities; the harmonic mean is not itself a joint probability.')
report.append('### Soft associations and structural interventions\n\n'+table(['Feature','Aligned n','Aligned date %','Aligned MSMI %','Unaligned n','Unaligned date %','Unaligned MSMI %'],[(k,d.get('1',{}).get('n',0),fmt(100*d['1']['date_rate']),fmt(100*d['1']['msmi_rate']),d['0']['n'],fmt(100*d['0']['date_rate']),fmt(100*d['0']['msmi_rate'])) for k,d in audit['public']['soft_associations'].items()]))
report.append('The snapshot sample has too few positive terminal outcomes to identify a statistically credible single strongest driver. Conversations has the largest positive point-estimate contrast, while lifestyle’s observed contrast reverses; neither is a causal finding. Administrative pending outcomes are excluded unless resolved or old enough to mature. Snapshot soft fields may have been revealed after assignment, so these tables are descriptive rather than prospective prediction validation.\n\n'+table(['Conversations aligned, pace aligned','Mature/resolved known pairs','MSMI %'],[(k,d['n'],fmt(100*d['msmi_rate'])) for k,d in audit['public']['conversations_pace_interaction'].items()]))
report.append('The simulator has exact category equality for pace and conversations, with no graded topic concordance or pace tolerance. In the structural model their contributions are additive on the introduction logit; nonlinearity produces probability-scale interaction. Controlled interventions hold other latent values fixed and integrate shared Gaussian effects over 1,398 feasible pairs per regime:\n\n'+table(['Regime','Goal effect','Pace effect','Lifestyle effect','Conversations effect','Conversations×pace'],[(k,*[fmt(100*d['mean_terminal_probability_effect'][f]) for f in ('relationship_goal','relationship_pace','lifestyle','conversations')],fmt(100*d['conversations_pace_mean_probability_interaction'])) for k,d in funnel['feature_interventions'].items()])+'\n\nEffects are percentage-point differences in qualified terminal probability. Goal is strongest in development; pace is strongest in shift. This is causal evidence within the invented structural simulator, not evidence about real relationships.')
report.append('### Missingness and feasibility topography\n\nThe exact public declined-hard share is 700/2,000=35%. Mean ages are 33.841 for declined members and 33.542 for others; declined gender counts are 309 women, 334 men and 57 nonbinary members. Their zone counts are 405/167/103/25 for a/b/c/d. Missingness is generated independently of preference truth conditional on completeness; these demographics do not establish a demographic refusal mechanism. Eligibility and query allocation prune any hard-declined node. Seven policy tests and all simulator action validators check this invariant.\n\n'+table(['Pool','Visible feasible edges','Active feasible edges','Visible islands degree≤1','Max visible degree','Bipartite'],[(d['pool'],d['all_visible_graph']['edges'],d['active_graph']['edges'],d['all_visible_graph']['islands'],d['all_visible_graph']['max_degree'],d['all_visible_graph']['bipartite']) for d in audit['public']['pools']]))
report.append('Public snapshots cannot identify the true post-query graph for permanently unknown fields without leakage. A separate offline generated-world audit compares day-0 graphs before and after free resolution of all non-declined constraints, plus the all-arrival truth graph:\n\n'+table(['Family','Before edges','After non-declined resolution','All-arrival truth edges','Truth islands','Truth max degree'],[(v,fmt(mean(r['before']['edges'] for r in rows)),fmt(mean(r['after_unlimited_non_declined_constraints']['edges'] for r in rows)),fmt(mean(r['truth_graph_all_arrivals']['edges'] for r in rows)),fmt(mean(r['truth_graph_all_arrivals']['islands'] for r in rows)),max(r['truth_graph_all_arrivals']['max_degree'] for r in rows)) for v,rows in audit['offline_graph_audit'].items()]))
report.append('All generated truth graphs in this audit have zero nodes connected to more than half the pool: there are no empirical “super-spreaders” by the requested definition. Full degree histograms, densities and component counts are serialized in `audit.json`; a hard query can expose constraints but cannot repair a genuine isolated island.')
report.append('## 4. Funnel delays, survival and censoring\n\n`audit.json` contains Kaplan–Meier net survival and Nelson–Aalen cause-specific cumulative hazard for all four requested transitions, with risk sets, events, competing failures and administrative censoring. It also contains Aalen–Johansen event incidence. Permanent no-response and cancelled dates are competing outcomes. Treating them as ordinary noninformative censoring would overstate observed conversion probability. Full follow-up funnel curves by policy, variant and seed are in `funnel_audit.json`.\n\n![Public survival and incidence](results/research/figures/survival.png)')
loss=[]
for p in ('greedy','full','product'):
 rs=[r for r in funnel['episodes'] if r['policy']==p];n=sum(r['observed_both_second_yes'] for r in rs);ld=sum(r['late_date'] for r in rs);lf=sum(r['late_feedback'] for r in rs);overlap=sum(r['both_late'] for r in rs)
 loss.append((p,n,ld,lf,overlap,fmt(100*(ld+lf-overlap)/max(1,n))))
report.append(table(['Policy','Both second yes','Date >30d','Feedback >3d','Both failures','Disqualified % among both yes'],loss)+'\n\nThese are exact realized counts over five seeds and six variants. Zero observed late-date losses does not mean the structural risk is zero: the exact delayed tail beyond 30 days is 2.1866%. Conditional on both yes submissions, the probability at least one response is late is 64%. Busy lockout can reach 39 days; the recorded per-episode busy mean and maximum are in the funnel audit. Exact conditional day-60 completion cutoffs are 51 and 43 for standard and delayed respectively. Unconditional cutoffs depend on pair quality, and neither is an official stopping deadline.\n\n![Exact timing distributions](results/research/figures/timing.png)')
report.append('## 5. Architecture, ablations and statistical evidence\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  JSON[Public JSON observations] --> FILTER[Decline and availability pruning]\n  FILTER --> ASK[Budgeted potential-degree queries]\n  ASK --> REFRESH[Evaluator refreshes fields]\n  REFRESH --> LEARN[Observed-response logistic update]\n  LEARN --> DFM[Pending-response mixture EM]\n  DFM --> SCORE[Directional reciprocal ranking]\n  SCORE --> THRESHOLD[Temporal and local-degree reservation]\n  THRESHOLD --> GRAPH[Verified general compatibility graph]\n  GRAPH --> BLOSSOM[500 ms bounded blossom]\n  BLOSSOM --> OUTPUT[Legal pairs and JSON memory]\n  BLOSSOM --> FALLBACK[Greedy on failure or timeout]\n  FALLBACK --> OUTPUT\n```\n\nThe full variant uses potential-degree hard queries and verified-neighbor soft queries, a diagonal logistic approximation, response-stage delayed-mixture EM, harmonic reciprocal ranking and general-graph blossom. UCB-style bonuses encourage unobserved potential nodes; they are not calibrated UCB confidence bounds. The frozen variant changes only fusion to product. Features are snapshotted when assigned, and later queries cannot rewrite training data. Second feedback is a separate target and is not incorrectly appended to introduction-response training. Limitations: terminal multipliers are uncalibrated, no full multistage conversion EM or Thompson sampler is claimed, diagonal posterior uncertainty ignores shared dyadic effects, and the threshold is a heuristic rather than an exact Bellman solution.')
report.append('The default threshold declines to zero by day 35 and scales by minimum endpoint degree. An additional evaluated `hazard` configuration uses T=.024×(60−t)/60×(1−h_t)^8×min(1,min degree/4), with the correct prior conditional departure hazard. This supplies the requested horizon/hazard/local-thickness combination without pretending unavailable statuses reveal exits. Its score is '+fmt(mean(r['msmi_per_100_arrived_members'] for r in hazard['episodes']))+'. The terminal score remains a ranking approximation rather than calibrated P(MSMI).')
report.append('### Full-policy head-to-head, official subprocess measurements\n\n'+table(['Policy','MSMI/100','Coverage %','Mutual acceptance % of assigned','Dates % of mutually accepted','Ask cost','Mean call ms'],[(p,fmt(ss['overall'][p]['mean']),fmt(100*mean(r['coverage'] for r in sub['episodes'] if r['policy']==p)),fmt(100*mean(r['mutual_acceptance_rate'] for r in sub['episodes'] if r['policy']==p)),fmt(100*mean(r['date_completion_rate'] for r in sub['episodes'] if r['policy']==p)),fmt(mean(r['ask_cost'] for r in sub['episodes'] if r['policy']==p)),fmt(mean(r['mean_inference_ms'] for r in sub['episodes'] if r['policy']==p))) for p in ('greedy','no_asks','random','full','product')]))
report.append('Rates are episode means, not pooled-ratio estimates; denominators are stated explicitly. Detailed scenario statistics for all six requested metrics, standard deviations and 95% t intervals are in the corresponding `*_statistics.json` files. Official primary score averages families equally.\n\n'+table(['Family','Greedy','No asks','Random','Full architecture','Product'],[(v,*[fmt(stats['scenario_summaries'][p][v]['msmi_per_100_arrived_members']['mean']) for p in ('greedy','no_asks','random','full','product')]) for v in ('development','sparse','cold_start','delayed','shift','drift')]))
cs={c['policy']:c for c in stats['comparisons']}
report.append('### Component ablation matrix\n\n'+table(['Configuration','MSMI/100 mean','Seed-cluster SD','95% CI','Paired t p vs greedy','Holm p'],[(p,fmt(d['mean']),fmt(d['sd']),f"[{fmt(d['ci95'][0])}, {fmt(d['ci95'][1])}]",fmt(cs[p]['paired_t_p']) if p in cs else '—',fmt(cs[p]['holm_p']) if p in cs else '—') for p,d in stats['overall'].items()]))
report.append('`greedy_engine` changes only allocation. `hungarian` forces men versus everyone else and uses true Hungarian assignment plus dummy unmatched columns; it loses legal within-side edges. `fifo`, `soft_only`, `no_active_asks` change clarification. `static` and `zero` change reservation. `product` and `unilateral` change fusion; unilateral uses member-list direction rather than a symmetric predictor. `no_learning` and `no_dfm` isolate learning and pending-response correction. `batch3/5/7` clear on days divisible by 3/5/7, while still querying daily. `hard15` forbids soft queries for the first 15 days. The matrix is one-factor ablation, not a full factorial interaction study. Paired component contrasts against the full architecture are also saved in `benchmark_vs_full.json`, and paired query contrasts in `query_comparison_vs_query_degree.json`.\n\nSeparate five-seed query comparisons: '+', '.join(p+'='+fmt(d['mean']) for p,d in qs['overall'].items())+'. Entropy uses exact public-generator prior entropy of missing semantic hard fields conditional on visible age/zone, restricted to constraints bundles and followed by common soft fill. Spectral expansion uses optimistic added edges and exact lambda_2, usually zero because disconnected components remain. It is not an exact posterior expected-connectivity optimizer.')
report.append('### Fresh-seed frozen candidate\n\n'+table(['Policy','MSMI/100 mean','Seed-cluster SD','95% CI'],[(p,fmt(d['mean']),fmt(d['sd']),f"[{fmt(d['ci95'][0])}, {fmt(d['ci95'][1])}]") for p,d in hs['overall'].items()]))
hc=next(c for c in hs['comparisons'] if c['policy']=='product')
report.append(f"Product minus greedy is {fmt(hc['difference']['mean'])} MSMI/100; its 95% paired interval is [{fmt(hc['difference']['ci95'][0])}, {fmt(hc['difference']['ci95'][1])}]. Paired seed-cluster t p={fmt(hc['paired_t_p'])}; exact seed sign-flip p={fmt(hc['exact_seed_signflip_p'])}. Gains are **not statistically significant at .05**. With five seed clusters, a two-sided exact sign-flip test cannot attain p below 2/32=.0625 even if every difference has the same sign. The t test adds distributional assumptions. Common seeds correlate scenario families, so we cluster across the six families within seed rather than declaring 30 independent trials. Exploratory comparisons receive Holm correction. More seeds are required for a credible superiority claim; no result is relabeled significant to satisfy the directive.\n\n![Exploratory and fresh-seed scores](results/research/figures/scores.png)")
report.append('## 6. Scenario-specific findings\n\n'+table(['Family','Diagnosis','Executed countermeasure / conclusion'],[
 ('sparse','Twelve geographically disconnected zones plus hard-filter islands','3/5/7-day local-compatible clearing epochs tested; no universal batching benefit. Global lambda_2 cannot value local gains.'),
 ('cold_start','Few verified edges initially; no query can repair hard decline','Hard-first 15 days tested against normal mixed spending. Potential-degree and entropy-like acquisition compared; no blanket 100% hard-spend dominance proved.'),
 ('delayed','Long lockouts reduce repeat opportunities; small relative date tail','Exact delay tail and busy durations audited. Early global stopping would sacrifice valid late introductions within follow-up.'),
 ('shift','Lifestyle coefficient reverses; pace dominates','Response-only online adaptation and no-learning ablation tested. Reliable per-episode sign detection is not established.'),
 ('drift','Assignment-day logit drops at day 35','Daily versus 3/5/7-day clearing and temporal thresholds tested; report actual front-loading below, not a purported optimal rate.'),
 ('development','Sparse graph and rare terminal positives','Blossom optimizes modeled one-step weights; no claim of global dynamic optimality.')]))
report.append('Measured fraction of introductions assigned before day 35:\n\n'+table(['Policy','Development %','Sparse %','Cold start %','Delayed %','Shift %','Drift %'],[(p,*[fmt(100*sum(sum(d['assignments'] for d in r['daily'] if d['day']<35) for r in funnel['episodes'] if r['policy']==p and r['variant']==v)/max(1,sum(r['metrics']['assignments'] for r in funnel['episodes'] if r['policy']==p and r['variant']==v))) for v in ('development','sparse','cold_start','delayed','shift','drift')]) for p in ('greedy','full','product')]))
report.append('The randomized shift experiment uses 80 replications per sample size with independent fully observed logistic trials. Detection powers are '+', '.join(f"N={d['n']}: {100*d['detection_probability']:.1f}%" for d in audit['shift_detection']['randomized_experiment'])+'. The optimistic information-envelope normal planning estimate is 1,386 labels for one-sided 95% confidence with 95% power. Adaptive feedback is clustered and incomplete, so this is not a guarantee for deployed learning. The executed benchmark cannot support a universally sufficient N or an online 95% confidence claim.')
report.append('## 7. Production audit and failure runbook\n\nThe image was built successfully and executed offline using `evaluate.docker_command`. Effective cgroups show CPU quota/period 200000/100000=2 cores, memory.max=1,073,741,824 bytes and pids.max=64. UID is 65534; root filesystem write fails with errno 30 (read-only filesystem). Network mode is none and only loopback is up; this kernel additionally lists inactive tunnel devices. The image contains only `kit.py` and `research_policy.py` in /app. Its inspected size is recorded in `image_inspect.json` and asserted below the 2 GiB image limit. The baseline `.dockerignore` allowlist was expanded only for these inference files and the research Dockerfile.')
